From fed5a5554cff6809576b96b661a461cb7e6daf5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:35:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/17] engine: pipelined solo decode beside --batch slots and
 spec lanes for 2-4 users in shared VRAM (STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE,
 STRATA_SPEC_LANES, STRATA_LC_SHARE, our 81015495 0238f7f8 7db06746 1edbfdb9
 ee403737 abdc40fb f60f4ea5)

Production's final form (f60f4ea5; nothing later touches it). One commit for both: since abdc40fb the solo
pipeline and the lanes are one mechanism (lanes_may folds the solo pipeline in, the lanes carve the solo
pipeline's verifiers' arenas and hold its snapshots, and the boot captures its graphs for the lanes' rule).

v0.2.12 specifics:
- STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE and upstream's STRATA_PW_WITH_BATCH lift the same "not with --batch slots" gate: one or
  the other (both set: a told-once line, upstream's path as upstream wrote it). batch_blocks_pw itself is
  unchanged, so mtp_first stays false under the solo pipeline (the lanes need the drafter on the last card).
- lanes_may and lanes_asked share one more refusal (lanes_upstream_off, said once at boot): STRATA_PIPED_MTP,
  STRATA_PIPED_CONCURRENT (pump() runs inside that read), DFlash2 (--draft dflash2 / auto) and
  STRATA_PW_WITH_BATCH. The drafter block's refusal names DFlash2 slot drafts when batch_df2_wanted is the cause.
- stage_room: the lanes' reserve is taken off stage_reserve::room_bytes (the header is left alone); solo_pl_snap
  comes off both later-stage room reads (also the head-to-host retry).
- BSlot reuses upstream's dprob (kVerifyNarrowT; the lanes refuse DFlash2, its other user).
- pl_drain returns its error; its new PlSnap side-stream sync runs only with STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE.
- ee403737: overlap_gate refuses live / held lanes; the KVS disjointness check counts the lane drafters' K/V.
- The lane-side VRAM numbers (STRATA_LC_LAZY_MIB 141, kLaneOwnMib/kLaneShareMib 120/40, lane_cost 28/41 MiB)
  and kVramSafeMib (512) are production's, not yet recalibrated for v0.2.12 (needs a boot log and a soak).

All env names and defaults as in production; with every switch off the paths are v0.2.12's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
