+// STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE=1 (read once; off by default): --pipeline-windows 2 beside --batch slots.  A request the engine
+// decodes on the solo path (GEN: the server's lone request) runs the pipelined decode loop (two verifiers per stage,
+// its windows overlapped across the stages) instead of the serial one; batch admissions (BGEN's first token), the slots'
+// windows and every prompt read stay as they are.  Without --pipeline-windows it asks for 2 when --batch is on.
+// STRATA_SPEC_LANES=2..4 (read once; off by default): spec lanes beside the pipelined slot groups.  When two to N of
+// the lane slots (0, GS, 2 GS, 3 GS: where the server puts the first users) decode and nothing else, each runs as its
+// own solo-MTP stream - its own verifier per stage on the slot's sessions, its own drafter - and the streams' windows
+// interleave on the stages; otherwise the batch pump as before (strata/program/spec_lanes.hpp).  It folds the solo
+// pipeline in (STRATA_SOLO_PIPELINE, unless that says otherwise) where the lanes can run: one user decodes pipelined on
+// the solo path.  The lanes' verifiers share the arenas of verifiers idle while they run (STRATA_LC_SHARE: the default
+// for 3 and 4).  0: off; -1: not supported.
+int spec_lanes_env() {
+    static const int n = strata::program::spec_lanes::env_lanes(std::getenv("STRATA_SPEC_LANES"));
+    return n;
+}
+// `lanes_may`: the configuration lets the lanes run (the checks known before the split's stages are made; review: a
+// configuration that refuses the lanes does not get the solo pipeline folded in - its second verifiers, snapshots and
+// reserve - from STRATA_SPEC_LANES alone).  Read once per value.
